WEBVTT

00:03.960 --> 00:09.320
So now let's understand how the database server executes the subqueries behind the scenes.

00:09.320 --> 00:09.800
Let's go.

00:09.800 --> 00:14.400
So now let's say that you are a data analyst and you are writing a query at the client side where you

00:14.400 --> 00:16.680
have a subquery inside the main query.

00:16.680 --> 00:18.960
So once you go and execute it, what's going to happen.

00:18.960 --> 00:23.040
The database engine is going to go and identify the subquery.

00:23.040 --> 00:26.880
And in this situation the database is going to execute first the subquery.

00:26.880 --> 00:31.320
So here the subquery is like selecting and retrieving data from the table orders.

00:31.320 --> 00:37.360
So that means the database has to retrieve the data from the disk storage from the user data.

00:37.360 --> 00:43.480
So now once the subquery is executed the result the intermediate result is going to be stored in the

00:43.480 --> 00:44.040
cache.

00:44.040 --> 00:49.640
So this means the result of the subquery is temporary and as well very fast to retrieve.

00:49.680 --> 00:54.680
And now once the database engine is done with the subquery it's going to go and start executing the

00:54.680 --> 00:55.560
main query.

00:55.560 --> 01:00.040
So let's see in this scenario it's completely depending on the result of the subquery.

01:00.040 --> 01:04.440
So that means the main query is going to go and interact with the cache storage.

01:04.440 --> 01:09.160
So this means now the data can be retrieved very fast from the result of the subquery.

01:09.200 --> 01:12.760
Once it's done it's going to forward the result to the database engine.

01:12.760 --> 01:16.320
And the database engine can forward the results to the client side.

01:16.320 --> 01:19.080
And at your side you will find the final result.

01:19.080 --> 01:24.440
And of course, once everything is executed, the database engine is going to go and clean up the cache

01:24.440 --> 01:29.720
so the subquery results can be destroyed and removed completely from the cache in order to have a free

01:29.720 --> 01:31.560
space for other queries.

01:31.560 --> 01:35.800
So this is how the database server executes the subqueries behind the scenes.
